					<div class="xsmall">12/20/2000 - 8:35 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=245">Nikanj</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=721">Muldin</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I'm not sure why there are so many people leaving, but I assume it must be because their goals are not the same as the guild's.  It's too bad.  Frankly, I agree with the guild's principles of helping each other and gernally making the game more enjoyable.  Sure, maybe if I'm TPing people all over norrath, I won't level as fast, but there's more to the game than just getting that next level.<br />
<br />
I've been out of town for the past couple of days, so I haven't been on EQ or reading the board, and now I come back and see so much fighting, and even Chumlee thinking about leaving.  Most of you don't know this, but I came from a guild that was basically disbanded due to people leaving and a general loss of interest in the guild.  I really hope that the same thing doesn't happen to PotD.  I know that I'll be sticking with the guild as long as I can.<br />
<br />
Well, that's been my ramblings for today :)<br />
btw, I'll try to make it to the Dalnir event (I put myself as an attendee), but since it is being held on Christmas Eve Day, I don't know how much I'll be able to play.  And I'm certainly not getting up at 3am (CST) when it supposedly starts, but I'll try my best to get there at some point during the day (probably won't be there until the afternoon CST).<br />
<br />
--<br />
Nikanj						</td>
